  {
   "n": 11,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>There are four water tanks each with equal capacity of 1200 liters. The water is being pumped&nbsp;from one tank to another as per the following scheme.<br>From P to Q at the rate 52 liters/second<br>From P to S at the rate 48 liters/second<br>From Q to R at the rate 36 liters/second<br>From R to P at the rate 76 liters/second<br>From R to S at the rate 24 liters/second<br>From S to Q at the rate 48 liters/second<br><br></p>\n<p>If all the pumps are started simultaneously when each of the tanks has 384 liters of water, which&nbsp;tank would get emptied first?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>P</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>Q</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>R</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>S</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p><img src=\"media/dc/dcfc8a56014b7e91466b.png\"></p>\n<p>Now, let&rsquo;s calculate the net flow of the water in each of the tanks.<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; P : 76 &ndash; 100 = &ndash;24 litres/second<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Q : 100 &ndash; 36 = 64 litres/second<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; R : 36 &ndash; 100 = &ndash;64 litres/second<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; S : 72 &ndash; 48 = 24 litres/second<br>It shows that R gives away 64 liters/second, so will be emptied first and the time taken<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; =&nbsp; &nbsp; 384/64 = 6 seconds</p>"
  },
