  {
   "n": 14,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>The average of 26, 29, <em>n</em>, 35 and 43 lies between 25 and 35. If n is always an integer and greater&nbsp;than the average of the given integers, then the value of <em>n </em>is</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>33 &lt; <em>n </em>&lt; 47</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>34 &lt; <em>n </em>&lt; 43</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>33 &lt; <em>n </em>&lt; 42</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>None of these</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>Average of 26, 29, 35 and 43 is 33.25. Also the average of 26, 29, <em>n</em>, 35 and 43 lies between 25 and&nbsp;35 i.e.,</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/87/8765344347ea89adf524.png\"></p>\n<p>Since the value of <em>n </em>is an integer and greater than 33.25,<br>then 33 &lt; <em>n </em>&lt; 42</p>"
  },
